  "note": "Triennial election of 15 January 1923, the first after proportional representation was abolished; Portadown was divided into three wards (North 5 seats, South-East 4, South-West 6) by a Ministry of Home Affairs order of 31 October 1922 (Belfast Gazette, 10 November 1922). Messrs Campbell, Copeland, Corbett, Locke, Moffett, G. Johnston, W. J. Johnston and Mrs M'Cammon were the official nominees of the Labour Unionist Association; \"all the other candidates were Independent Unionists\". Counted 16 January. South-West Ward: no contest; the six were returned unopposed (Rock, Courtney, Gregory and Wright were members of the old council). David Rock: no party label printed in 1923. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, Armagh County Council, 26 May 1927, printed 'U': Armagh Guardian, 3 June 1927, p. 3 (\"New Co. Council: Portadown Apathy in Voting\"); Lurgan Mail, 4 June 1927, p. 4 (\"County Armagh Election\")). His labels elsewhere differ (UUP x1, Labour Unionist x1)."
